        "2378": {
            "name": "Text.014",
            "parent": "2344",
            "components": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": {
                        "text": "GO 2D PLAY\n\nTo play Musica11y.net you first have to \ncreate a musical instrument, \n\nThere are two ways to create a musical\ninstrument. \n\nIn Edit Mode\n1: First select a space on the grid, then \nselect a note on the left. The note you \nselect populates the grid location.\n\n2: Select a note value on the left\nthen select a point on the grid\nto populate. Repeat as you wish.\n\nTo cler a note, select \"clear note\" and\nthen select the note on the grid you \nwish to clear. You can clear all if needed.\n\nYou can populate the while grid at once \nusing the FILL button on the left. Select\n a Hex note, then select fill populate with \ngrid with notes in the chosen Hex key.\n\nYou can change scale by shosing another\nHex key and press FILL. Or you can select\nSCALES to bring up options for more scale \noptions.\nChange what Hex Keys are shown using\nthe KEY button.\n\n\n",
                        "alignment": "left",
                        "verticalAlignment": "top"
                    }
                }
            ],
            "translation": [
                -0.0016464,
                -0.1590451,
                -0.0000239
            ],
            "rotation": [
                0.0,
                -0.0,
                -0.0,
                1.0
            ],
            "scaling": [
                0.46221,
                0.6,
                0.6
            ]
        },
